            <ArticleTitle>[Effects of work conditions in coal mines on prevalence of ischemic heart disease among miners].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>19-23</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Occurrence of coronary heart disease among workers of Donbass coal mines more than 2 times exceeds the values for matched general population (groups of males aged 20-49). Peculiarities of working environment and industrial process were proved to be risk factors for coronary heart disease among the miners.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
